Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sana po itong itatanong ko ng mga taga-PINAC.

752
00:54:27,910 --> 00:54:34,030
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sinisilip ko po yung ating mga targets ng NHSP ng 2027.

753
00:54:34,750 --> 00:54:37,090
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At tinitinan ko rin po yung gaps.

754
00:54:37,570 --> 00:54:41,090
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Particularly po halimbawa as basic as condoms.

755
00:54:41,890 --> 00:54:48,510
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kailangan po natin 1.2 million condom beneficiaries would require up to 302.4 million annually.

756
00:54:48,510 --> 00:54:49,370
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Lubrikans po.

757
00:54:49,810 --> 00:54:54,510
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kailangan natin ang shortfall po ay up to 98.7 million.

758
00:54:54,730 --> 00:54:56,910
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So medyo glaring po yung gaps.

759
00:54:57,010 --> 00:55:04,250
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So even HIV self-testing, ang shortfall po ay nasa 26 to 63.9 million na shortfall.

760
00:55:04,390 --> 00:55:11,670
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So ano pong ginagawa natin given na domestic funding na po karamihan na majority po natin sa HIV procurement?

761
00:55:11,850 --> 00:55:19,210
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: How will the Department of Health ensure that the 2027 budget is actually sufficient to meet the NHSP targets?

762
00:55:19,570 --> 00:55:20,150
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Chair.

763
00:55:20,150 --> 00:55:21,390
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Please wind up.

764
00:55:22,450 --> 00:55:24,550
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The Deputy Minority Leaders.

765
00:55:24,730 --> 00:55:31,910
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So una po talaga medyo po yung aming procurement kailangan po talaga mag-improve.

766
00:55:32,110 --> 00:55:37,750
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi yung pong commodities ang primary ano po dyan eh para ma-reach natin itong ating mga targets.

767
00:55:38,430 --> 00:55:45,810
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung isa po rin po ay papalawakin na po natin sa PhilHealth yung ating coverage po ng OHAT kaya na nasabi ko kanina.

768
00:55:46,230 --> 00:55:47,190
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: To include PrEP.

769
00:55:47,630 --> 00:55:49,310
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: To include even the testing.

770
00:55:50,110 --> 00:55:51,990
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So 2 prong po through YACAP.

771
00:55:51,990 --> 00:55:53,090
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Through the OHAT.

772
00:55:53,410 --> 00:55:54,710
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Through the OHAT.

773
00:55:54,730 --> 00:55:55,730
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Program.

774
00:55:55,930 --> 00:55:58,590
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: And then DOH po talagang dito sa commodities.

775
00:55:59,790 --> 00:56:01,630
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mabilis lamang po for the last question.

776
00:56:01,790 --> 00:56:04,310
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Salamat po at tanagaabang ating mga key population.

777
00:56:04,830 --> 00:56:10,390
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Pag-usapan po natin yung supply and chain management kasi nababalitaan po namin ang daming failure sa ating logistics.

778
00:56:10,910 --> 00:56:11,930
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Last question Mr. Chair.

779
00:56:12,530 --> 00:56:18,730
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Bakit po sa ating NEP pare-parehong 10 million na allocation para sa lahat ng regions para ting sa supply and chain management?

780
00:56:19,090 --> 00:56:22,850
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: 10 million sa NCR, 10 million sa Central Visayas, 10 million sa Caraga.

781
00:56:22,850 --> 00:56:24,690
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: E given po yung geographic.

782
00:56:24,730 --> 00:56:30,230
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Character of these regions, sigurado po tayo hindi pare-pareho yung requirements when it comes to logistics.

783
00:56:30,570 --> 00:56:34,130
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ano pong science behind this 10 million allocation across all regions?

784
00:56:34,790 --> 00:56:36,450
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay, that will be the last question.

785
00:56:37,290 --> 00:56:40,190
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: DML, Secretary, please respond.

786
00:56:40,590 --> 00:56:42,590
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Nakita ko rin po yun bakit pare-pareho.

787
00:56:42,730 --> 00:56:47,170
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Iba-iba naman yung site, yung geographic layout nung kada region.

788
00:56:47,890 --> 00:56:52,450
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero ang sabi po ay dahil sa warehousing which is common daw for all the regions.

789
00:56:52,450 --> 00:56:54,490
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero gaya po nang nasabi ko.

790
00:56:54,730 --> 00:56:58,430
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Nag-aaralan din namin po paano nga po ito maging mas efficient.

791
00:56:58,950 --> 00:57:02,510
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At ano po yung variability factors na kailangan po nating i-consider.

792
00:57:03,430 --> 00:57:09,950
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: E nababother po kasi tayo sa mga ganyang klase na allocation kasi sigurado po tayo hindi yan batay doon sa evidence at pangangailangan ng region.

793
00:57:10,210 --> 00:57:11,130
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Salamat Mr. Chair.

794
00:57:11,570 --> 00:57:17,230
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maraming salamat DML Sendanya for your very valuable and significant questions.

795
00:57:17,670 --> 00:57:24,650
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: We now move to the majority. May I recognize Representative Adrian.

796
00:57:24,730 --> 00:57:25,230
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Amatong.

797
00:57:25,230 --> 00:57:27,230
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Thank you very much Mr. Chair.

798
00:57:27,230 --> 00:57:27,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Please proceed.

799
00:57:27,730 --> 00:57:29,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Good morning po sa buong DOH family.

800
00:57:29,730 --> 00:57:39,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Gusto ko lang pong itanong kasi pag may nakakausap akong mga legislators sa ibang bansa lagi sila nagugulat sa healthcare system natin.

801
00:57:39,730 --> 00:57:45,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi meron tayong sa PhilHealth, meron tayong may yakap at saka ano-ano pang mga programa.

802
00:57:45,730 --> 00:57:53,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Bakit po hindi natin mapag-isa so that kung mga kasi minsan may mga programs tayo na hindi na nga maintindihan ng mga constituents natin eh.

803
00:57:53,730 --> 00:57:55,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Ako nga minsan may ibang hindi ko maintindihan eh.

804
00:57:55,730 --> 00:58:03,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So bakit po hindi nalang isang healthcare system, isang programa na kung saan malaki yung nakukuha ng mga constituents natin?

805
00:58:03,730 --> 00:58:05,730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Ba't ang gulo-gulo pa po?

806
00:58:05,730 --> 00:58:12,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Tama po yan dahil sa pag-aaral nga po ng Philippine Institute of Developmental Studies.

807
00:58:12,240 --> 00:58:22,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kapag ang payment po ay siloed, may iba-ibang pinagkukunan. May PhilHealth, may galing po sa DOH, may galing po sa DSWD-IX.

808
00:58:22,240 --> 00:58:24,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Humihina po yung leverage ng atin.

809
00:58:25,240 --> 00:58:33,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung ito po ay ang mandato ng mga laman po mag-cover at magbayad ay PhilHealth.

810
00:58:33,240 --> 00:58:44,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung ito po ay unti-unti nating ma-ecentralize, yung leverage po natin, halimbawa na magbago po yung payment natin to what you call prospective, parang pakyawan.

811
00:58:44,240 --> 00:58:52,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Inumpisahan na po namin, kaya po maaaring nabalitaan nyo may mga private hospital na po na naglalaanong kama nila sa NBB.

812
00:58:52,240 --> 00:58:54,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yun po kasi nagagamit na po namin.

813
00:58:54,240 --> 00:58:58,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Nagagamit na po namin yung ating purchasing leverage and purchasing power.

814
00:58:58,240 --> 00:59:02,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero ngayon po, pag siloed po ang payment, medyo mahina po yun.

815
00:59:02,240 --> 00:59:07,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya nga po, unti-unti na namin pinag-aaralan paano po i-consolidate under PhilHealth.

816
00:59:07,240 --> 00:59:11,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Obviously, nabanggit nyo pa, may mga studies.

817
00:59:11,240 --> 00:59:18,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Can we work together so that we can come up with a solution so that we can consolidate everything and make it easy for our constituents?

818
00:59:18,240 --> 00:59:22,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi kawawa, naguguluhan sila minsan eh. Tapos minsan ang tagal pang maningil.

819
00:59:22,240 --> 00:59:23,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Ang second question ko po.

820
00:59:23,240 --> 00:59:24,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Sa PhilHealth.

821
00:59:24,240 --> 00:59:29,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi yung mga constituents ko, lagi silang nagtatanong, bayad kami ng bayad sa PhilHealth.

822
00:59:29,240 --> 00:59:33,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Pero pag na-hospital kami, konting-konti naman yung nakukuha namin sa PhilHealth.

823
00:59:33,240 --> 00:59:35,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: In fact, napag-usapan before eh.

824
00:59:35,240 --> 00:59:42,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: And I also agree na dapat hindi nakalodge ang mga politiko ang medical assistance kasi minsan napo-politika.

825
00:59:42,240 --> 00:59:48,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: As much as we want that to happen, ang problema kasi, pag lumalapit sa amin yung constituents namin,

826
00:59:48,240 --> 00:59:52,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: kapiranggot lang yung sinasagot ng PhilHealth, eh syempre ipaglalaban namin na pwede rin naming matulungan.

827
00:59:52,240 --> 00:59:53,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Di ba po?

828
00:59:53,240 --> 00:59:59,240
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Sir, in the last two years po, halos doble na po yung...

829
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:01,400
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: naging coverage ng PhilHealth.

830
01:00:01,520 --> 01:00:04,060
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: But we recognize, for certain cases,

831
01:00:04,260 --> 01:00:07,920
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: lalo na yung mga pasyente na mas malubha yung kondisyon,

832
01:00:08,180 --> 01:00:09,880
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: kulang pa rin yung bayad doon.

833
01:00:10,160 --> 01:00:14,000
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So meron pong parte ng pinag-aaralan namin sa benepisyo namin,

834
01:00:14,180 --> 01:00:17,380
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: yung tinatawag na DRG or may modifier po.

835
01:00:17,380 --> 01:00:20,440
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Ngayon po, kahit ikaw ay may high blood,

836
01:00:20,620 --> 01:00:24,380
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: 60 years old na kunwari, na mas maraming sakit,

837
01:00:24,640 --> 01:00:28,320
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: kung nagka-say dengue ka, same lang po yung bayad ng PhilHealth sa inyo

838
01:00:28,320 --> 01:00:31,200
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: versus someone na very young and healthy.

839
01:00:31,660 --> 01:00:35,240
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Parang yun yung klarong-klaro na dapat medyo magkaiba po

840
01:00:35,240 --> 01:00:36,820
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: or may adjustments po yung bayad.

841
01:00:36,920 --> 01:00:39,100
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So meron na pong pag-aaral na nangyayari doon.

842
01:00:39,940 --> 01:00:43,580
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And that is supposed to inform how we adjust the payments further.

843
01:00:44,380 --> 01:00:49,720
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Second, sir, is clearly we have to work with the public hospitals

844
01:00:49,720 --> 01:00:53,700
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: whose 90% of bids should really be no balance billing.

845
01:00:54,000 --> 01:00:57,080
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And merong mechanism po yung mga public hospitals

846
01:00:57,080 --> 01:01:01,800
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: to get additional budget from LGU as well as additional MAIFIP, etc.,

847
01:01:01,800 --> 01:01:04,680
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: for example, na dapat at the end of the day,

848
01:01:04,800 --> 01:01:08,040
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: nakaka-uwi yung pasyente na wala po siyang extra na binayad.

849
01:01:08,100 --> 01:01:12,480
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So I think those are clearly implementation challenges

850
01:01:12,480 --> 01:01:16,520
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: that we have to work with on top of rates adjustment

851
01:01:16,520 --> 01:01:17,660
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: that we'll have to work on.

852
01:01:17,740 --> 01:01:24,380
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: But we definitely agree with you, sir, na lalo na now that also the premium is higher,

853
01:01:24,920 --> 01:01:26,880
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: our members expect na mas malakas,

854
01:01:27,080 --> 01:01:28,400
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: kaya din naman talaga yung coverage.

855
01:01:29,400 --> 01:01:31,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Na-appreciate ko po yung sagot nyo.

856
01:01:31,560 --> 01:01:33,340
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Ang problema ko lang po kasi,

857
01:01:33,740 --> 01:01:36,000
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: pag nakikita ng mga constituents natin,

858
01:01:36,260 --> 01:01:37,860
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: na example yung sa PhilHealth Board,

859
01:01:38,020 --> 01:01:41,300
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: pag nakita nila yung benefits na nakakuha ng mga members ng board,

860
01:01:41,700 --> 01:01:42,500
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: sabi, ang lalaki.

861
01:01:42,960 --> 01:01:47,300
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos pag narinig nila na may surplus na, may savings na ang PhilHealth,

862
01:01:47,400 --> 01:01:49,040
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: kaya kinuha daw ng national government,

863
01:01:49,460 --> 01:01:50,100
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: hindi na naman itin yan.

864
01:01:50,320 --> 01:01:51,680
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Paano nagkakaroon ng surplus?

865
01:01:51,900 --> 01:01:54,160
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Eh, hindi naman kami natutulungan ng maayos.

866
01:01:54,160 --> 01:01:57,000
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: That is something that is very, very hard to explain,

867
01:01:57,080 --> 01:01:58,700
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: to those na nangangailangan.

868
01:01:58,820 --> 01:02:00,900
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Lalo na pag pag-need na nila, pag na-hospital siya,

869
01:02:00,980 --> 01:02:02,400
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: tapos kapiranggot lang.

870
01:02:02,520 --> 01:02:05,540
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos they end up begging from politicians for help.

871
01:02:05,660 --> 01:02:07,840
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kaya nga sa office namin, tinanggal namin yung,

872
01:02:08,100 --> 01:02:09,140
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: don't talk to me.

873
01:02:09,420 --> 01:02:11,300
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Ang staff natin, pag nakita nangangailangan kayo,

874
01:02:11,380 --> 01:02:12,180
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: tutulungan kayo agad.

875
01:02:12,700 --> 01:02:16,860
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: I hate it when constituents go to politicians and need to beg.

876
01:02:17,580 --> 01:02:20,520
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Parang nakakawalan ng dignidad.

877
01:02:21,180 --> 01:02:23,500
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Unfortunately, hindi lang natin kaya pondohan lahat.

878
01:02:23,500 --> 01:02:26,920
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kaya nga po sana may mas maayos na sistema so that PhilHealth,

879
01:02:26,920 --> 01:02:28,640
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: they can fund as much as they can.

880
01:02:30,240 --> 01:02:34,800
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And then, definitely sir, we know that the hospital bill is partly made up of

881
01:02:34,800 --> 01:02:37,240
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: hospital fees and professional fees.

882
01:02:37,440 --> 01:02:42,240
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, alam din po namin sa lahat ng discussions with our legislators na

883
01:02:42,240 --> 01:02:44,700
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: the PF is also a big challenge.

884
01:02:44,960 --> 01:02:50,040
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And so, Sec. Edwin has already started and we will continue

885
01:02:50,040 --> 01:02:53,460
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: our discussions po with the professional societies.

886
01:02:54,060 --> 01:02:56,860
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Lalo na kung magbigyan natin ng PhilHealth,

887
01:02:56,920 --> 01:02:59,520
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: plus more predictable, ma-EFIP,

888
01:02:59,880 --> 01:03:05,160
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: ano yung ways for the healthcare professionals to make their PFs din

889
01:03:05,160 --> 01:03:07,100
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: a little bit more predictable, diba?

890
01:03:07,280 --> 01:03:10,980
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Para hindi tayo lahat magkagulatan kung magkano yun.

891
01:03:11,440 --> 01:03:15,100
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And siguro lastly, sir, we also recognize na

892
01:03:15,100 --> 01:03:19,520
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: while a lot of improvements have been done the last 18 months

893
01:03:19,520 --> 01:03:21,220
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: under Sec. Edwin and PhilHealth,

894
01:03:21,620 --> 01:03:25,420
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: we also know that many of the providers sometimes,

895
01:03:25,640 --> 01:03:26,900
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: because mahirap yung process,

896
01:03:26,920 --> 01:03:34,300
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: hindi na nila ginagamit yung PhilHealth to enroll kung ano yung condition ng patient.

897
01:03:34,620 --> 01:03:38,120
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, ma-EFIP na lang gagamitin nila kasi mas mahirap yung proseso.

898
01:03:38,440 --> 01:03:43,400
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, yun din naman po yung commitment namin to make it easier for healthcare providers

899
01:03:43,400 --> 01:03:47,100
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: to be part of the benefit packages that we have

900
01:03:47,100 --> 01:03:51,660
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: and also to make our frontline services for them much easier.

901
01:03:52,080 --> 01:03:52,640
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Thank you po.

902
01:03:53,080 --> 01:03:55,020
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Nabanggit po kanina yung sayakap.

903
01:03:55,020 --> 01:03:58,140
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos, may mga kalukuhan na naman sa YACAP eh.

904
01:03:58,140 --> 01:04:03,140
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Yung mga LGUs, kasi sabi niyo nga minsan na-e-enroll yung mga tao na hindi nga nila alam eh.

905
01:04:03,260 --> 01:04:06,200
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos, nagagamit yung pondo na intended for them na hindi nila alam eh.

906
01:04:06,680 --> 01:04:08,220
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So, ano po yung safeguards natin dito?

907
01:04:11,880 --> 01:04:19,540
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, definitely, sir, we will be coming up with our parang YACAP 2.0 enhanced policies

908
01:04:19,540 --> 01:04:25,140
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: and that's a result of all the consultations and all the feedback that's coming from the ground.

909
01:04:25,140 --> 01:04:26,540
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, for example,

910
01:04:26,540 --> 01:04:32,340
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: part of this would include really institutionalizing yung liveness check,

911
01:04:32,720 --> 01:04:37,540
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: meaning may verification na yung patient, biometrics,

912
01:04:37,920 --> 01:04:40,120
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: para po malaman na yun yung actual patient.

913
01:04:40,280 --> 01:04:45,160
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Second is, mas malalaman nung member kung ginamit ba siya.

914
01:04:45,300 --> 01:04:50,620
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, ngayon po, makikita nyo sa EGOV app na may YACAP provider na kayo, etc.

915
01:04:51,140 --> 01:04:54,480
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Nalalagay po dyan kung may claim kayo sa inpatient.

916
01:04:54,660 --> 01:04:56,480
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, soon enough, ilalagay natin.

917
01:04:56,580 --> 01:05:03,540
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, ito nga din po namin kung yung provider ay nag-claim on your behalf dahil YACAP mo sila.

918
01:05:03,900 --> 01:05:08,380
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, kung hindi mo pala alam, then actually malalaman din ng pasyente, no?

919
01:05:08,380 --> 01:05:14,760
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, many other similar mechanisms will be put in place as well as CAP

920
01:05:14,760 --> 01:05:20,020
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: in terms of ano lang yung kaya ng isang provider na alagaan.

921
01:05:20,020 --> 01:05:25,960
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So, kunwari po ngayon, medyo may default tayo, everything can go through the LGU.

922
01:05:26,420 --> 01:05:26,520
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: But,

923
01:05:26,540 --> 01:05:33,460
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: But as we move forward, we want to be able to discuss with each province, citywide health system

924
01:05:33,460 --> 01:05:42,280
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: and say, ngayon po ang kapasidad po ng probinsya ninyo ay alagaan sa 300,000 of the 500,000 constituents.

925
01:05:42,900 --> 01:05:46,640
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Ano pong gagawin natin dun sa 200,000 remaining?

926
01:05:46,640 --> 01:05:51,660
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Tate po, pilitin natin sa lahat ng health center nyo pa rin sila ma-assign.

927
01:05:51,960 --> 01:05:56,500
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Pero kung hindi po sila ma-accommodate, unfair naman yun sa pasyente.

928
01:05:56,800 --> 01:06:05,580
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So we want to work with the LGUs, not to force them to become healthcare providers

929
01:06:05,580 --> 01:06:11,060
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: but to get them to be the conveners of the providers in their locality.

930
01:06:11,060 --> 01:06:17,960
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: And say, itong 200,000 na ito, meron bang private non-for-profit na pwedeng tumulong sa kanila

931
01:06:17,960 --> 01:06:23,840
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: to operate certain yakap centers in the interim and maybe in two years time

932
01:06:23,840 --> 01:06:26,520
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: with HFEP, with HealthU,

933
01:06:26,540 --> 01:06:32,660
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: with Human Resource Support, kaya na ni LGU yun, babalik na po yung mga pasyente nun kay LGU.

934
01:06:32,800 --> 01:06:38,640
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So para lang din po fair sa pasyente na where PhilHealth is paying for their services,

935
01:06:38,900 --> 01:06:41,220
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: they should get the right services po.

936
01:06:42,160 --> 01:06:46,860
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Meron po kami na reklamo dati na mayor sa amin kasi dun sa PhilHealth program,

937
01:06:47,240 --> 01:06:50,960
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: ang ginawa niya, he gathered a lot of people dun sa hospital niya,

938
01:06:51,260 --> 01:06:56,300
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: tapos pinakain, pinabaunan, pinapirma, tuwan-tuwan yung mga tao,

939
01:06:56,540 --> 01:06:58,180
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: pala nila, natulungan sila.

940
01:06:58,420 --> 01:07:02,100
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Pag uwi nila, yung PhilHealth pala nila, ano na, sagad na.

941
01:07:02,840 --> 01:07:07,280
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos, ang problema ko lang po sa PhilHealth, hindi naman nila hinabol yung mayor ngayon.

942
01:07:08,120 --> 01:07:11,940
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So ngayon, mukhang sa AKAP, mukhang yun din ang mangyayari eh.

943
01:07:12,020 --> 01:07:16,020
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So I hope yung grievance mechanism natin is designed in such a way na

944
01:07:16,020 --> 01:07:20,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: hahabulin talaga natin yung mga taong umaabuso.

945
01:07:20,620 --> 01:07:24,340
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi ang sama ng logo sa PhilHealth eh, kasi kaya nga nakabalik na mayor yun ngayon

946
01:07:24,340 --> 01:07:25,480
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: kasi hindi naman nila hinabol.

947
01:07:25,780 --> 01:07:26,500
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Sinara yung hospital.

948
01:07:26,540 --> 01:07:29,380
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Yung hospital niya, head ng hospital niya, pinanagot.

949
01:07:29,520 --> 01:07:33,820
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Pero yung pinaka-utak nung ginawa, eh hindi naman pinanagot.

950
01:07:58,780 --> 01:08:01,340
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Spirit and individual, dun po sila lahat.

951
01:08:01,580 --> 01:08:02,600
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Yun yung parang entry point.

952
01:08:02,760 --> 01:08:08,640
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: So we have to do it well because that will be the entry point for Filipinos and to the health system po.

953
01:08:08,800 --> 01:08:09,320
PhilHealth President and CEO Dr. Beverly Lorraine Ho: Thank you.

954
01:08:10,260 --> 01:08:13,680
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: I'd like to understand more yung programa ng AKAP po

955
01:08:13,680 --> 01:08:18,880
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: and why ito yung parang, kinasabi niyong base program natin para ma-integrate lahat.

956
01:08:19,340 --> 01:08:25,560
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Because if there is anything we can do to legislate for that, please, please tell us.

957
01:08:25,720 --> 01:08:28,080
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi we are desperate to find a way na,

958
01:08:28,780 --> 01:08:32,320
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: para makaawa yung mga constituents natin for medical assistance.

959
01:08:32,500 --> 01:08:34,600
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi kawawang-kawawa na nga sila.

960
01:08:34,760 --> 01:08:39,380
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos parang nakakawala ng dignidad kasi yung kailangan pang magmakaawa para matulungan.

961
01:08:39,740 --> 01:08:43,580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Sana po magtulungan tayo para at par naman tayo sa ibang mga bansa.

962
01:08:43,720 --> 01:08:45,220
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi pinagtatawa naman tayo minsan eh.

963
01:08:45,240 --> 01:08:48,940
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: May nakausap po two weeks ago sa lihan kong conference.

964
01:08:49,200 --> 01:08:52,100
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Sabi nila, bakit ka pa may medical assistance?

965
01:08:52,280 --> 01:08:53,560
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Eh yung healthcare system yun.

966
01:08:53,860 --> 01:08:55,200
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Wala akong masagot eh.

967
01:08:55,200 --> 01:08:58,240
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi ako mismo parang hindi ko maintindihan yung healthcare system natin.

968
01:08:58,780 --> 01:08:59,500
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Magtulungan tayo.

969
01:08:59,660 --> 01:09:01,020
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Sana po ma-solve natin yun.

970
01:09:01,500 --> 01:09:05,440
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Ang last ko po is, sana i-remind natin yung mga hospitals na,

971
01:09:06,120 --> 01:09:10,200
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: di ba dapat ang first contact ng mga pasyente is yung medical social worker.

972
01:09:10,680 --> 01:09:14,580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: May mga hospitals na hindi yung medical social worker yung unang nakakausap nila eh.

973
01:09:14,660 --> 01:09:20,160
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kaya prone tuloy sa mga abuses ng mga kalukohan minsan ng doctors or ng mga hospitals.

974
01:09:21,100 --> 01:09:24,040
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay, please wind up, Congressman Amatong.

975
01:09:25,500 --> 01:09:28,000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Phil Health, DOH, please reply.

976
01:09:28,460 --> 01:09:28,660
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you.

977
01:09:28,780 --> 01:09:37,200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes po eh, kasi kailangan nga merong skills to assess yung capability or yung social status ng ating pasyente.

978
01:09:38,020 --> 01:09:53,400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kasi nga po doon sa pag-seset nga po ng rules ng ano naman po, MIFIP, pinag-usapan na po namin, may iba pong hospital na may classification ABCDE, depende po doon sa social class, yung dami po nung pwedeng ibigay ng MIFIP.

979
01:09:53,400 --> 01:09:57,400
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ano po namin yan, i-institutionalize po namin.

980
01:09:57,400 --> 01:10:04,740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At dapat po yung talagang trained na mga social worker or at least po merong certification ang pwedeng magbigay ng assessment.

981
01:10:05,460 --> 01:10:13,220
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Since may time ba po, ang last issue ko po, ang DOH minsan, mga regional offices nyo, pag nagre-reklamo kami tungkol sa bad practices ng mga hospitals,

982
01:10:13,400 --> 01:10:17,400
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: lagi nilang sinasabing na wala silang position na sawayin yung mga hospitals.

983
01:10:17,600 --> 01:10:22,180
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Sana naman po, meron din kayong ano na pwedeng yung sitahin yung mga hospitals who are not doing well.

984
01:10:22,180 --> 01:10:27,020
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Because, so umpisa pa lang, if they're not doing well, mas mabuti nang masita natin para masolve natin kaagad.

985
01:10:27,400 --> 01:10:41,800
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Sige po, actually po, meron kaming corporate action center sa PhilHealth na yun po yung pinagdudulugan ng mga reklamo at meron na po po kaming sistema ngayon pa paano po i-triage, kumbaga.

986
01:10:42,340 --> 01:10:46,240
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Mag-uusap po kami na gamitin din po yung platform na yun for hospitals.

987
01:10:46,660 --> 01:10:50,320
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Maraming salamat po. Maraming salamat din po sa tulong nyo sa Liloid General Hospital. Thank you.

988
01:10:50,580 --> 01:10:51,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Salamat din po.

989
01:10:51,580 --> 01:10:54,460
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maraming salamat, Congressman Amatong.

990
01:10:55,240 --> 01:10:58,640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And, Secretary, may hotline po ba?

991
01:10:58,680 --> 01:11:05,700
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: May hotline po yung inyong central response center para mayaman po ng lahat kung may mga complaint?

992
01:11:11,560 --> 01:11:15,440
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Alam ko po yung 1555. 1555 po.

993
01:11:15,700 --> 01:11:23,880
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, any complaints sa hospitals, public and private, pwede tumawag sa 1555.

994
01:11:25,540 --> 01:11:30,700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero yun nga po, parang meron lang po kaming ilang mga seats.

995
01:11:31,340 --> 01:11:33,380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya gusto namin i-professionalize.

996
01:11:33,640 --> 01:11:39,960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: I-professionalize na isa talagang call center, kahit third party yung mag-engage, na nabibigyan kami ng datos po.

997
01:11:40,360 --> 01:11:42,500
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya nag-uusap na po kami pa paano pag-isahin.

998
01:11:43,560 --> 01:11:53,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, I think everyone is looking forward to the efficient operation of that response center, yung call center ng 1555.

999
01:11:54,380 --> 01:12:02,020
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, hopefully, dumating tayo doon para immediate yung maging response ng DOH at ng PhilHealth.

1000
01:12:02,020 --> 01:12:02,160
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you.

1001
01:12:03,640 --> 01:12:17,040
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: By the way, for the information of everyone, nilagay po natin sa special provision ng 2026 budget na pwede pong 100% sagutin ng professional fee, aside from the hospital bill.

1002
01:12:17,660 --> 01:12:24,380
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Nasa special provision po yan ng 2026 GAA para po alam ng lahat.

1003
01:12:24,380 --> 01:12:33,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, kailangan lang po natin siguro magkaroon ng number one, patanggap sa mga doctors, especially in the private sector.

1004
01:12:33,640 --> 01:12:36,020
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Minsan hindi nila tinatanggap, or most of the time.

1005
01:12:36,720 --> 01:12:42,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And yung CAP, kasi minsan nagiging runaway hospital bill and professional fee.

1006
01:12:42,400 --> 01:12:43,880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, I think we should work on that.

1007
01:12:45,160 --> 01:13:00,260
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ika may po, may nilabas po si former Secretary Ted niya po, Herbosa, na bagamat nandun po, nakapaloob doon sa 2026 yung 100% PF, ay maglalabas po kami nung mga patakaran.

1008
01:13:00,860 --> 01:13:03,460
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung ito po ay tinitingnan namin, ipapattern ba namin?

1009
01:13:03,640 --> 01:13:11,640
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: HMO, na meron kang RVU times multiple, or ito ba ay percentage of what PhilHealth is covering, X numbers of times.

1010
01:13:11,900 --> 01:13:13,500
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So, yun po yung aming pinag-aaral.

1011
01:13:14,060 --> 01:13:17,580
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Otherwise po, inflationary, nagdoble, nagtitriple po yung PF.

1012
01:13:17,660 --> 01:13:21,700
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, understood, Secretary. Maraming salamat. We will wait for the guidelines.

1013
01:13:22,520 --> 01:13:22,900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you.

1014
01:13:22,900 --> 01:13:33,630
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, we move back to the minority. May we recognize Assistant Minority Leader, Rep. Iris Montes.

1015
01:13:34,450 --> 01:13:35,350
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Ma'am, please proceed.

1016
01:13:35,370 --> 01:13:36,230
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1017
01:13:36,230 --> 01:13:37,110
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: You have five minutes.

1018
01:13:37,630 --> 01:13:39,530
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

1019
01:13:40,130 --> 01:13:51,430
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: On November 7 last year, this representation took the floor to deliver a privileged speech on the WHO's Global Tuberculosis Report for 2025.

1020
01:13:52,530 --> 01:14:03,690
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The report confronted us with the undeniable truth that we have consistently ranked fifth in the world in terms of TB ranking, third in 2025, third.

1021
01:14:03,690 --> 01:14:09,330
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And 100 Filipinos dying every single day because of TB.

1022
01:14:09,950 --> 01:14:13,390
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I know, Mr. Secretary, that you have not warmed your seat yet.

1023
01:14:13,390 --> 01:14:23,670
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But can you please inform us, what exactly did you inherit regarding the procurement of TB drugs?

1024
01:14:27,360 --> 01:14:35,280
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung anti-TB drugs nga po, at saka yung cartridges para dun sa gene experts.

1025
01:14:35,320 --> 01:14:38,680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ay talaga pong medyo na-delay yung procurement.

1026
01:14:39,060 --> 01:14:44,700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya nung nire-constitute nga namin yung back, medyo binigyan ko ng directive to really push.

1027
01:14:45,500 --> 01:14:57,960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Simultaneously po, nag-reach out kami dun sa mga ating mga foreign grant na pwedeng magbigay muna habang inaayos namin itong procurement.

1028
01:14:58,200 --> 01:14:59,560
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At may nagre-respond naman po.

1029
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:12,200
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: In fact, the Global Fund already committed to give us substantially, almost $159 million worth of medicines for TB, HIV, and malaria.

1030
01:15:12,320 --> 01:15:13,600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Bulk of it will be in TB.

1031
01:15:14,240 --> 01:15:22,700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ang issue lang po namin ay paano po ayusin na for the first time po, binigyan po ang DOH as procuring agent.

1032
01:15:22,700 --> 01:15:25,120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Hindi na po dadaan ng private third party.

1033
01:15:25,780 --> 01:15:29,300
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So kami po ay nag-ano kung paano po ayusin yung taxes.

1034
01:15:30,000 --> 01:15:40,700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: As I said, since we're already agency to agency, meron naman po kami pag-uusap initially ng DOF na i-relax po yung requirement na magbayad pa ng taxes kung agency to agency.

1035
01:15:41,080 --> 01:15:42,020
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So yun po yung inaayos.

1036
01:15:44,770 --> 01:15:51,870
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung current procurement timelines po, ang bid evaluation ay September 3 to 10, post-qual po ng September 11 to 22.

1037
01:15:51,870 --> 01:15:58,790
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At sana po ay ma-recommend na po for awarding by end September po.

1038
01:15:59,570 --> 01:16:01,870
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mr. Secretary, have you already...

1039
01:16:01,950 --> 01:16:16,910
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Have you already conducted some kind of a review kung ano po ba ang nangyari ng nakaraan, nagkaroon ng failure of bidding, ano po ba ang naging problema that we were not able to procure the much needed TB drugs?

1040
01:16:18,230 --> 01:16:24,830
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So ang inaayos ko lang po muna yung prospective kasi yung kailangan po nating bigyan po ng solusyon.

1041
01:16:25,330 --> 01:16:31,910
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero yun po ay binigay ko na po dun sa ating procurement service under USEC sa Kilabon na magbigay po ng recommendation.

1042
01:16:31,950 --> 01:16:33,430
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kung ano nga po yung nangyari.

1043
01:16:34,290 --> 01:16:44,110
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: When can we expect po kaya na ma-deliver yung mga TB drugs and all the needed equipment sa mga gene experts natin?

1044
01:16:44,830 --> 01:16:50,810
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So kung ma-award po by end of September, another one to two months po. So by end of October or by November.

1045
01:16:51,710 --> 01:16:58,570
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa 2027 budget po, did we include again budget for the procurement of TB drugs?

1046
01:17:02,780 --> 01:17:05,120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes po. This is on top of the global...

1047
01:17:05,500 --> 01:17:13,600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Global fund, ano po. Meron po tayo na 3.02 billion allocated for TB.

1048
01:17:14,440 --> 01:17:25,660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At nga ang isa rin po namin pinofocus are the for community-based setting, yung pinaka-congested na pinagmumula na maraming drug resistance at TB, which are people with PDLs.

1049
01:17:25,660 --> 01:17:27,660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Mga people with...

1050
01:17:28,940 --> 01:17:31,660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Ano nga yung liberty with...

1051
01:17:33,660 --> 01:17:34,660
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Tsaka po yung mga congested...

1052
01:17:35,500 --> 01:17:43,820
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Composted areas like workplace na tabi-tabi. So yun po yung ating pinofocus na magawan po kaagad ng screening.

1053
01:17:51,220 --> 01:17:59,380
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Isa pa rin po palang quick solution somehow, yung pong TB na pwede na pong i-avail sa gamot.

1054
01:18:00,420 --> 01:18:08,700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya meron po tayong gamot. For first-liner lang po yun, yung mga usual na triple, quadruple anti-cox or anti-TB meds.

1055
01:18:09,380 --> 01:18:10,700
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Pero yun pong for...

1056
01:18:12,100 --> 01:18:18,740
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: MDR, multi-drug resistance, tsaka XDR, DOH po yun. Kaya kasama po yun sa nakabudget.

1057
01:18:18,900 --> 01:18:22,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So sa DOH, yung procurement mo, meron for MDR and XDR.

1058
01:18:22,800 --> 01:18:22,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes.

1059
01:18:23,440 --> 01:18:33,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nabanggit niyo po, Secretary, yung tungkol sa Global Fund, no? So kayo na po ang directly magpo-procure, hindi na dadaan sa private sector?

1060
01:18:34,620 --> 01:18:36,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: O this time lang po? Ngayon lang kayo pinagbigyan?

1061
01:18:38,260 --> 01:18:40,840
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: First time po na ginawa po yan.

1062
01:18:41,020 --> 01:18:41,960
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Kaya we're working on the...

1063
01:18:42,100 --> 01:18:48,600
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung framework. Kahapon nga lang po, pinirmahan ko na yung how to move forward on discussion of the framework agreement.

1064
01:18:48,600 --> 01:18:57,000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But is it true that yung Global Fund po natin is tapering off consistently through the years? Tama po, di ba?

1065
01:18:57,540 --> 01:19:09,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ibig sabihin po, if it's tapering off, kailangan makompensate natin from our domestic financing to be able to compensate for whatever is lost. Tama po, Mr. Secretary?

1066
01:19:09,700 --> 01:19:11,540
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yes po. Kaya nga while we're transitioning.

1067
01:19:12,100 --> 01:19:16,680
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Palakas na ng PhilHealth yung coverage niya ng TB. Kasi doon po magta-transition.

1068
01:19:16,900 --> 01:19:21,840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So maraming salamat po. So in two months, we will be able to procure the TB drugs.

1069
01:19:22,300 --> 01:19:32,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Moving on po, on vaccines procurement. For 2026 po, ba did we procure vaccines? For instance, for influenza, pneumococcal vaccines, meron po ba tayong procurement?

1070
01:19:41,120 --> 01:19:48,120
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: Yung pong mga vaccines natin, actually carry over pa ng 2025. Kaya po ngayon lang na move.

1071
01:19:49,620 --> 01:20:10,160
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So delayed nga po, pero pinahabol din po rin po yung 2026. Doon po sa mga flu vaccine, kasi depende nga po yung doon sa kung ano po yung prevailing strain during the year, pwede pa naman po daw yung 2025 gamitin nga yung 2026.

1072
01:20:10,740 --> 01:20:19,040
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: So meron na po tayong na-award na pentavalent para doon sa mga bata at para doon sa immunization po ng pentavalent na mga bata.

1073
01:20:19,620 --> 01:20:33,480
Secretary Edwin M. Mercado: At saka ang flu vaccine pa ang pending, pero nabigyan na natin yung pneumococcal. Pneumococcal po ang na-award na rin po namin.

1074
